# runtime.school — PySpark Execution Engine Architecture

For PySpark, we need to build a real Apache Spark execution engine behind runtime.school. It cannot work exactly like our existing SQL or Python execution environments because Spark runs on the JVM, manages execution plans, uses partitions, and can start multiple worker processes.

The good news: we do not need to build our own Spark engine or operate a Databricks cluster for every learner. We can use Apache Spark itself, build our own execution and grading layer around it, and scale the infrastructure gradually.

